There's a certain mobile platform that requires apps to be able to
save their state without actually quitting before they are
backgrounded, and there's a chance that this app will either just be
killed without getting notified, or asked to just awake and continue
running in the state it was backgrounded.

So the vanilla dosave0() doesn't do it in that case, since it destroys
a lot of local state on the heap.

Is there a (not too complicated, coding-wise) way to rebuild that
destroyed state without a full restore from file?

